# Lamp udev roles. Tracked source: robots/lamp/rootfs/etc/udev/rules.d/, installed
# onto / at image build and on every device-profile OTA — edit HERE, not on the
# device, or the next OTA overwrites the hand edit.
#
# Every rule maps a vid:pid to a ROLE name (device-camera, device_speaker, ...)
# that /etc/asound.conf and /opt/hal/.env refer to, so a hardware swap is one
# line here and nothing else. Several vid:pid may fill the same role; only the
# one actually plugged in wins.

# Camera role -> /dev/device-camera (HAL_CAMERA_NAME). index==0 picks the capture
# node, not the UVC metadata sibling.
# SunplusIT OPENAICAM (also exposes a built-in mic, device_micro3)
SUBSYSTEM=="video4linux", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1bcf", ATTRS{idProduct}=="28cc", ATTR{index}=="0", SYMLINK+="device-camera"
SUBSYSTEM=="sound", ACTION=="change", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1bcf", ATTRS{idProduct}=="28cc", ATTR{id}="device_micro3"
# ZVCAI USB_Camera (current fit on lamp-ac82 / lamp-4ace / lamp-dbda, 2026-09)
SUBSYSTEM=="video4linux", ATTRS{idVendor}=="01da", ATTRS{idProduct}=="5875", ATTR{index}=="0", SYMLINK+="device-camera"
# ZVCAI USB_Camera (current standard fit, seen on lamp-ac82/4ace/dbda 2026-09)
SUBSYSTEM=="video4linux", ATTRS{idVendor}=="01da", ATTRS{idProduct}=="5875", ATTR{index}=="0", SYMLINK+="device-camera"

# Servo driver: QinHeng CH340 -> /dev/device-servo
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1a86", ATTRS{idProduct}=="55d3", SYMLINK+="device-servo"

# Voice mic: Jieli Technology -> ALSA card device_micro2
SUBSYSTEM=="sound", ACTION=="change", ATTRS{idVendor}=="4c4a", ATTRS{idProduct}=="4155", ATTR{id}="device_micro2"

# Speaker: TTGK Technology -> ALSA card device_speaker
SUBSYSTEM=="sound", ACTION=="change", ATTRS{idVendor}=="3302", ATTRS{idProduct}=="1292", ATTR{id}="device_speaker"

# C-Media Audio Adapter (Unitek Y-247A) -> ALSA card device_cmedia. One card,
# two roles: its capture side is the sensing mic (alias device_micro1) and its
# playback side is the speaker (alias device_speaker) — both in /etc/asound.conf.
# A card gets exactly one udev id, so the id is the HARDWARE, aliases are ROLES.
SUBSYSTEM=="sound", ACTION=="change", ATTRS{idVendor}=="0d8c", ATTRS{idProduct}=="0014", ATTR{id}="device_cmedia"
# When its control node appears, pin the hardware level and create the softvol
# "Speaker" control (see /etc/asound.conf) before hal.service restores volume.
SUBSYSTEM=="sound", ACTION=="add", KERNEL=="controlC*", ATTRS{idVendor}=="0d8c", ATTRS{idProduct}=="0014", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="lamp-cmedia-speaker.service"
